Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::a_card_that_keeps_reporting_busy_is_given_up_on_once_the_deadline_passes`.

The defect: the SD power-up deadline is scaled as if it were in nanoseconds, so a card that keeps
reporting busy is asked again and again for a thousand seconds rather than one.

Expected to fail: the assertion in `BusyForeverCard::write` that power-up sends at most one more
`ACMD41` or `CMD1` once the clock has passed the deadline.
diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/sd.rs
@@ -466,7 +466,7 @@
             return Ok(operation_conditions);
         }
         if host.registers_mut().now_microseconds().wrapping_sub(start)
-            > POWER_UP_DEADLINE_MICROSECONDS
+            > POWER_UP_DEADLINE_MICROSECONDS * 1_000
         {
             return Err(InitializationError::PowerUp(operation_conditions));
         }
